\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{CSD}, a black-box framework for per-axis style bias detection via NLI-gated content control, style-controlled rewriting, and position-controlled pairwise comparison (\S\ref{sec:method}).
    \item \textbf{The Likert Blindspot:} Likert scoring attenuates style bias signals that pairwise comparison detects---complete at moderate bias ($d \to 0$ at $n = 355$), ${>}60\%$ signal loss at stronger effects---across six judge$\times$axis configurations ($p < 0.001$ pairwise vs.\ $p > 0.17$ Likert), confirmed by seven statistical methods (Tables~\ref{tab:main_results}--\ref{tab:sensitivity}).
    \item \textbf{Per-axis confound decomposition:} GEE conditional analysis separates style from quality effects, showing verbosity is style-dominated (Style OR $8$--$13$, Orig OR ${<}1$), formality conditional, register judge-dependent---determining which estimates are directly interpretable and which require conditional analysis (Table~\ref{tab:gee}).
\end{itemize}

tool_args.new_string:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{CSD}, a black-box framework for per-axis style bias detection via NLI-gated content control, style-controlled rewriting, and position-controlled pairwise comparison (\S\ref{sec:method}).
    \item \textbf{Measurement-mode divergence with per-axis confound structure:} Likert scoring misses style preferences that pairwise comparison detects---complete at moderate bias ($d \to 0$ at $n = 355$), ${>}60\%$ signal loss at stronger effects---confirmed by seven statistical methods across four judges and three benchmarks (Tables~\ref{tab:main_results}--\ref{tab:sensitivity}). GEE conditional decomposition reveals qualitatively distinct confound structures per axis: verbosity is style-dominated (Style OR $8$--$13$, Orig OR ${<}1$), formality is a conditional effect, register is judge-dependent---determining which pairwise estimates are directly interpretable and which require decomposition (Table~\ref{tab:gee}).
    \item \textbf{Practical implication:} Likert-only audits miss style-driven preferences that propagate through pairwise-based alignment pipelines; bias audits should employ pairwise comparison with position control and per-axis decomposition to distinguish style-dominated from quality-confounded effects.
\end{itemize}

